SPECIAL={20:'Correct the decay-constant unit to s^-1 and distinguish it from half-life.',31:'RBE requires biological endpoint, reference radiation, dose and model context; do not assign a universal isotope constant.',35:'Specific activity is activity per mass of a defined chemical species at a stated reference time. Use a dedicated QC result, not the legacy ambiguous scalar.',36:'Molar activity is activity per amount of substance at a stated reference time. Store separately from specific activity.',60:'Distinguish formal molecular charge from pH-dependent averaged charge; use a contextual test for the latter.',93:'Separate administered mass and molar amount, identify total/labeled/unlabeled analyte, and record any conversion.',105:'The example of Lu-177 becoming Hf-177 describes nuclear decay, not metabolism. Do not copy it into a metabolite field.',108:'Use matched TAC time/activity arrays or individual timed measurements; a list of times is not a scalar measurement.',109:'Represent an uncertainty as a separate linked measurement with quantity identity, unit and uncertainty statistic; do not overwrite the activity value.',110:'Replace disease-name examples with anatomical identities; disease context belongs to condition or evidence.',112:'A TAC needs matched time and activity vectors, administration anchor and decay reference; one MBq value is not a curve.',113:'A reference-region TAC is its own curve linked to that region and the same administration.',126:'Residence time can denote TIAC in an explicitly stated dosimetry convention. Consolidate only after confirming definition, normalization and time integration.',129:'An anatomical target must not be identified by a disease name.',134:'The source definition describes an absorbed-energy fraction. Distinguish absorbed fraction from a fraction of total absorbed dose and specify the denominator.',142:'Split BED and EQD2 into separate model-derived quantities with radiobiological assumptions. Neither is an absorbed-dose alias.',160:'Correct the expansion of PhPID to Pharmaceutical Product Identifier; this identifies a pharmaceutical-product level, not a radiopharmaceutical-specific system.',163:'A labeled activity range is a product/protocol evidence assertion; an individual approved plan is a separate record. Do not copy illustrative ranges into defaults.',164:'A labeled or protocol mass range is reference evidence; actual administered compound mass is a different patient quantity.',175:'Radiation restrictions require a current jurisdictional/product protocol source; the spreadsheet example is not a default instruction.',180:'Resolve CPT versus HCPCS Level II; an A-prefixed example is not a CPT code. No source example is accepted as a validated billing mapping.',211:'Use an ISO 8601 timestamp with UTC offset. Do not interpret an ambiguous EST/EDT abbreviation without source confirmation.',247:'Individual PFS uses an endpoint origin/event/censor record; cohort median PFS is a reference-result test with statistic and population.',248:'Individual OS uses an endpoint origin/event/censor record; cohort median OS is a reference-result test with statistic and population.',289:'A data-sufficiency score requires a named rubric, version and evaluation context; no threshold is imposed.',298:'An AI-readiness score is not a validated scientific quantity without a rubric and evidence; no default is assigned.',299:'Ontology completeness depends on declared scope and rubric; it is not a universal percentage.',306:'Schema-level concept mappings use semantic_mapping; general ontology axioms are managed outside this operational record model.',308:'Do not force arbitrary ontology predicates into structural link labels or claim logical entailment.',318:'Value type and allowed values are dictionary/schema metadata; result_text is only for actual qualitative evidence, not a place to redefine types.',320:'Versioned allowed-value sets belong to the dictionary or external terminology; retain the definition source rather than ad hoc per-record enums.',328:'A deprecated concept replacement requires reviewed mapping provenance; it is not automatically exact equivalence.'}
